# Typography Law

**Principle:** Font sizes must scale responsively. Use `clamp()` for fluid scaling — no fixed px without responsive fallback.

## Font Sizes

- **Fluid:** `font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem)`
- **Avoid:** Fixed px without media query or clamp fallback

## Line Height

- **Body:** 1.4–1.7
- **Multi-line headings:** 1.5–1.7
- **Example:** `line-height: 1.6`

## Line Length

- **Desktop:** 45–75 characters
- **Mobile:** 35–50 characters

## Text Containment

```css
max-width: 100%;
overflow-wrap: break-word;
text-wrap: balance;  /* headings, short text */
text-wrap: pretty;  /* longer paragraphs */
```

**No stragglers:** Single words alone on a line are forbidden. Use `text-wrap: balance` or explicit line-break spans.

## Anti-Patterns

- Fixed font sizes without `clamp()` or media queries
- Single orphan words on their own line

## Project Reference

This project: `STYLE-GUIDE.md` §2, §17. Montserrat (headings/CTAs); Plus Jakarta Sans (body). All font-sizes use `clamp()`.
